---
import '../styles/global.css'
import { settingsBootScript } from '@lib/settings'
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro'
import { allLevels } from '@lib/levels'
import SeoHead from '../components/SeoHead.astro'
import { breadcrumbLd } from '@lib/seo'
import { HTML_LANG, href, translator, type Lang } from '@lib/i18n'

interface Props { lang?: Lang }
const { lang = 'en' } = Astro.props
const zh = lang === 'zh'
const t = translator(lang, {
  'about 1 s': '约 1 秒',
  'a few seconds': '几秒',
  'a few minutes': '几分钟',
  'about 12 s (downloads the digits once)': '约 12 秒（第一次会下载数字图片）',
  'about 2–3 min (downloads the digits once)': '约 2–3 分钟（第一次会下载数字图片）',
  'your model trains in about 2 min': '你的模型训练约 2 分钟',
})
const L = (p: string) => href(lang, p)

// the files a level asks you to run on your computer (served from /files/, see scripts/sync_files.py);
// level numbers and titles come from each lesson's frontmatter
const LOCAL: [string, string[], string][] = [
  ['numpy-to-pytorch', ['first_run.py'], 'about 1 s'],
  ['debugging', ['broken_train.py', 'check.py'], 'a few seconds'],
  ['lstm', ['boss.py'], 'a few minutes'],
  ['seq2seq-attention', ['boss.py'], 'a few minutes'],
  ['autoencoders', ['demo.py'], 'about 12 s (downloads the digits once)'],
  ['latents-and-dit', ['boss.py'], 'about 2–3 min (downloads the digits once)'],
  ['write-a-gpt', ['skeleton.py', 'skeleton_hints.py', 'check.py', 'check_weights.json'], 'your model trains in about 2 min'],
]
const bySlug = new Map((await allLevels(lang)).map((l) => [l.id, l.data]))
const local = LOCAL.map(([slug, files, time]) => {
  const d = bySlug.get(slug)
  return { label: d ? `${d.level} ${d.title}` : slug, slug, files, time: t(time) }
})
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang={HTML_LANG[lang]}>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <SeoHead title={`${t('Run it on your computer')} · LLM by Hand`}
      description={zh ? '安装 Python、NumPy 和 PyTorch，在你自己的电脑上运行各关下载的脚本。' : "Install Python, NumPy and PyTorch, and run a level's downloaded scripts on your own computer."}
      jsonLd={breadcrumbLd([['LLM by Hand', L('/')], [t('Run it on your computer'), L('/setup/')]])} page={{ kind: 'setup' }}
      alternates={{ en: '/setup/', zh: '/zh/setup/' }} />
    <script is:inline set:html={settingsBootScript} />
    <style>
      .wrap { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem 4rem; }
      .top { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; }
      .top .tools { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; }
      .crumb { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--dim); text-decoration: none; }
      .crumb:hover { color: var(--accent); }
      h1 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.2rem); margin: 0.3rem 0 0.2rem; }
      .lede { color: var(--dim); margin: 0 0 1.5rem; max-width: 62ch; }
      h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 2.2rem 0 0.5rem; }
      p, li { max-width: 66ch; }
      pre { font-size: 0.85rem; }
      pre code { white-space: pre; }
      .os { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr)); gap: 0.8rem; }
      .os div { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem; background: var(--card); min-width: 0; }
      .os h3 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
      .os p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; }
      .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
      td code { white-space: nowrap; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <SiteHeader current="setup" />
    <div class="wrap">
      {zh ? (<>
      <h1>在你的电脑上运行</h1>
      <p class="lede">大多数关在浏览器里就能做，什么都不用装。有几部分要在你自己的电脑上运行：
        用 PyTorch 训练真实模型的 Boss 关，以及几个可选的运行。这些只需设置一次，大约十分钟。</p>

      <h2>1. 拿到文件</h2>
      <p>每个要在你电脑上运行的部分，都会给出它需要的文件链接，比如 <code>boss.py</code>。建一个课程文件夹，
        在里面为每一关各建一个文件夹。把这一关的文件下载到它的文件夹里，这一关的所有命令都在这个文件夹里运行。
        第 6 步的表格列出了所有文件。</p>
      <p>在那个文件夹里打开一个终端。终端是一个用来输入命令的窗口。在 macOS 上，它是“终端”这个应用
        （应用程序 → 实用工具）。在 Windows 上用 PowerShell（在开始菜单里）。在终端里，
        <code>cd</code> 后面跟上文件夹的路径，就会进入那个文件夹。</p>

      <h2>2. 安装 Python</h2>
      <p>你需要 Python 3.10 或更新的版本。先看看你装的是哪个版本：</p>
      <pre><code>python3 --version</code></pre>
      <div class="os">
        <div><h3>macOS</h3><p>从 python.org 安装，或者用 Homebrew：<code>brew install python</code>。</p></div>
        <div><h3>Windows</h3><p>从 python.org 安装，并勾选“Add python.exe to PATH”。之后凡是本页写 <code>python3</code> 的地方，都改用 <code>py</code>。</p></div>
        <div><h3>Linux</h3><p>用你的包管理器，比如 <code>sudo apt install python3 python3-venv</code>。</p></div>
      </div>

      <h2>3. 建一个虚拟环境，安装需要的包</h2>
      <p>虚拟环境是这门课专用的一个装包的文件夹，这样就不会和电脑上的其他东西冲突。只需建一次，
        建在放各关文件夹的那个文件夹里（比如 <code>llm-by-hand/</code>）：</p>
      <pre><code>python3 -m venv .venv
# Windows 上用：  .venv\Scripts\activate
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install numpy torch</code></pre>
      <p>环境激活后，命令提示符的开头会出现 <code>(.venv)</code>。打开新的终端时，先再运行一次
        <code>source</code> 那一行，再开始做课程。</p>

      <h2>4. 运行一个脚本</h2>
      <p>环境激活后，进入这一关的文件夹，运行里面的文件。比如支线 N4：</p>
      <pre><code>cd lstm          # 放 boss.py 的文件夹
python boss.py</code></pre>
      <p>脚本会把它们生成的文件（训练好的模型、下载的数字图片）写到这个文件夹里，或者写到你主目录下的一个缓存里。</p>

      <h2>5. CPU、NVIDIA GPU 还是 Apple GPU</h2>
      <p>所有内容在普通 CPU 上都能运行。有些脚本找到更快的设备时会用它：在有 NVIDIA 显卡的电脑上用
        <code>"cuda"</code>，在 Apple 芯片（M1 或更新）的 Mac 上用 <code>"mps"</code>，否则用
        <code>"cpu"</code>。可以这样查看 PyTorch 能用哪些设备：</p>
      <pre><code>python -c "import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available(), torch.backends.mps.is_available())"</code></pre>

      <h2>6. 所有可以运行的文件，以及要花多久</h2>
      <p>时间是在一台较新的笔记本上测的；没有 GPU、只用 CPU 时可能慢 2–3 倍。</p>
      <div class="scroll">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>关卡</th><th>文件</th><th>时间</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {local.map((d) => (
              <tr><td>{d.label}</td><td>{d.files.map((f, i) => (<>{i > 0 && '、'}<a href={`/files/${d.slug}/${f}`}><code>{f}</code></a></>))}</td><td>{d.time}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>7. 出了问题怎么办</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>“command not found: python3”</b>：Python 没有安装，或者不在 PATH 里。回到第 2 步（在 Windows 上试试 <code>py</code>）。</li>
        <li>安装时出现 <b>“externally-managed-environment”</b>：你是在虚拟环境之外安装。先运行 <code>source .venv/bin/activate</code> 那一行。</li>
        <li><b>torch 装不上</b>：先升级 pip（<code>pip install --upgrade pip</code>），再检查你的 Python 是 64 位的，而且不比 PyTorch 支持的最新版本更新。还是不行的话，安装只用 CPU 的版本：<code>pip install torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu</code>。在浏览器里做的关完全不需要 torch。</li>
        <li><b>下载很慢</b>：pip 可以从离你更近的镜像下载。用
          <code>pip install -i &lt;镜像地址&gt; numpy torch</code>，填上你所在国家的一个 PyPI 镜像的地址。</li>
        <li><b>“No module named numpy”</b>（或 torch）：这个终端里没有激活环境。再运行一次 <code>source</code> 那一行。</li>
        <li><b>脚本很慢</b>：Boss 关训练的是真实模型，花几分钟是正常的（见上面的表格）。</li>
      </ul>
      </>) : (<>

      <h1>Run it on your computer</h1>
      <p class="lede">Most levels run in your browser and need nothing installed. A few parts run on your own computer:
        the bosses that train real models with PyTorch, and a few optional runs. Set this up once; it takes about ten minutes.</p>

      <h2>1. Get the files</h2>
      <p>Each part that runs on your computer links the files it needs, for example <code>boss.py</code>. Make one course folder,
        and inside it one folder for each level. Download that level’s files into its folder, and run every command for that level in that folder.
        The table in step 6 lists every file.</p>
      <p>Open a terminal in that folder. A terminal is a window where you type commands. On macOS it is the app
        Terminal (Applications → Utilities). On Windows use PowerShell (from the Start menu). In the terminal,
        <code>cd</code> followed by the folder’s path moves you into the folder.</p>

      <h2>2. Install Python</h2>
      <p>You need Python 3.10 or newer. Check what you have:</p>
      <pre><code>python3 --version</code></pre>
      <div class="os">
        <div><h3>macOS</h3><p>Install from python.org, or with Homebrew: <code>brew install python</code>.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Windows</h3><p>Install from python.org and check the box “Add python.exe to PATH”. Then use <code>py</code> where this page says <code>python3</code>.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Linux</h3><p>Use your package manager, for example <code>sudo apt install python3 python3-venv</code>.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h2>3. Make a virtual environment and install the packages</h2>
      <p>A virtual environment is a private folder of packages for this course, so nothing conflicts with the rest of your
        computer. Make it once, in a folder that holds your level folders (for example <code>llm-by-hand/</code>):</p>
      <pre><code>python3 -m venv .venv
# on Windows use:  .venv\Scripts\activate
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install numpy torch</code></pre>
      <p>When the environment is active, your prompt starts with <code>(.venv)</code>. In a new terminal, run the
        <code>source</code> line again before working on the course.</p>

      <h2>4. Run a script</h2>
      <p>With the environment active, go into the level’s folder and run the file there. For example, for level N4:</p>
      <pre><code>cd lstm          # the folder that holds boss.py
python boss.py</code></pre>
      <p>The scripts write their own files (a trained model, downloaded digits) into that folder or into a cache in your home folder.</p>

      <h2>5. CPU, NVIDIA GPU or Apple GPU</h2>
      <p>Everything works on a plain CPU. Some scripts use a faster device when they find one: <code>"cuda"</code> on a
        computer with an NVIDIA graphics card, <code>"mps"</code> on a Mac with an Apple chip (M1 or newer), otherwise
        <code>"cpu"</code>. You can check what PyTorch sees with:</p>
      <pre><code>python -c "import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available(), torch.backends.mps.is_available())"</code></pre>

      <h2>6. Every file you can run, and how long it takes</h2>
      <p>Times on a recent laptop; a CPU without a GPU can be 2–3× slower.</p>
      <div class="scroll">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>level</th><th>files</th><th>time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {local.map((d) => (
              <tr><td>{d.label}</td><td>{d.files.map((f, i) => (<>{i > 0 && ', '}<a href={`/files/${d.slug}/${f}`}><code>{f}</code></a></>))}</td><td>{d.time}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>7. If something goes wrong</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>“command not found: python3”</b>: Python isn’t installed or isn’t on your PATH. Go back to step 2 (on Windows, try <code>py</code>).</li>
        <li><b>“externally-managed-environment”</b> when installing: you are installing outside the virtual environment. Run the <code>source .venv/bin/activate</code> line first.</li>
        <li><b>torch fails to install</b>: update pip first (<code>pip install --upgrade pip</code>), and check that your Python is 64-bit and not newer than the newest version PyTorch supports. If it still fails, install the CPU-only build: <code>pip install torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu</code>. The browser levels don’t need torch at all.</li>
        <li><b>Downloads are very slow</b>: pip can download from a mirror closer to you. Use
          <code>pip install -i &lt;mirror URL&gt; numpy torch</code>, with the address of a PyPI mirror in your country.</li>
        <li><b>“No module named numpy”</b> (or torch): the environment isn’t active in this terminal. Run the <code>source</code> line again.</li>
        <li><b>A script is slow</b>: the bosses train real models, so minutes are expected (see the table above).</li>
      </ul>
      </>)}
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
